    "updated_at": "2023-10-16T14:35:00Z",
    "body": "`Sec-` makes sense if the header is meant to be forbidden.\r\n\r\nI can't speak directly to the extensible priorities spec since I was mostly an observer while the process went through but the end-to-end header intentionally allows for overrides by the origin and it's not immediately clear that the intent wasn't also to allow for the value to be application-specified or at least overridden.\r\n\r\nThat said, it wouldn't hurt for both groups to align on when `Sec-` should be used and when it shouldn't. It also [came up](https://lists.w3.org/Archives/Public/ietf-http-wg/2023JulSep/0102.html) during discussions on compression dictionaries.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
